{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, thanks for reporting this. I found the cause: your account got locked this morning after several sign-in attempts failed in a row. Once an account is locked, the VPN, Outlook and Teams all refuse your password, even when it's the right one. I've asked a technician to unlock it. I'll let you know once they approve it, and after that you should be able to connect to the VPN and approve the Duo push as usual. To stop it locking again: (1) check whether your phone's mail app, Teams, or another device has an old saved password, and update it if so. (2) When you sign in, type your password carefully, and check Caps Lock and your keyboard layout. If it still fails once you're unlocked, or you think you may have forgotten your password, reply here and we can arrange a reset. The new password would be given to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "KB-013 checks: account status LOCKED (failed_login_count 5), vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false. Duo enrolled (duo_push, Tom's phone). Sign-in logs: 5 failed_password on 2026-10-09 between 09:42 and 09:57 ET. All were app m365 from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, during usual hours. No mfa_denied, no hosting networks, no new locations. The previous 9 sign-ins all succeeded with Duo (corporate, plus residential 198.51.100.24 for VPN). This looks like user error or a stale saved credential, not an attack, so KB-031 does not apply. Password last set 2026-07-21, so this was not a recent password change. Per KB-001, unlock_account is queued (approval id 1). No password reset requested because the user says he knows the password. If it fails after the unlock, consider reset_password with phone delivery. Escalate if it locks again within an hour after saved passwords are updated.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
